From 3cdbfb0352d3ce895ca07d20e88f32e0a462ea87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: starbite <starbite@local>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:07:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] patch: 0321-sweet-shared-cache-slide-16k.patch

arm64e (iOS 26) shared cache on the 4 KiB, non-PAC kernel:
- slide info v3/v5: authenticated pointers were only written back under
  ptrauth_calls; without PAC the rebased pointer was dropped and the chained
  value stayed in memory (launchd jumped through 0x86be6afc6e6389f0).
- shared region pager: v5 slide pages are 16 KiB; the loop assumed slide
  pages <= PAGE_SIZE and slid a 4 KiB page as if it were 16 KiB (copying
  past it). Each 4 KiB page is now slid inside its 16 KiB slide page,
  assembled from the backing object (sweet_sr_slide_subpage).
- starlte_smp.c (0300): st_cpu_survey only walks the CPUs this boot has (cpus=4 asserted in cpu_to_processor(4))
---
 bsd/dev/starlte_smp.c             |   3 +-
 osfmk/vm/vm_shared_region.c       |   6 ++
 osfmk/vm/vm_shared_region_pager.c | 111 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 119 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

